Z||000000||Eric||06-11-2001||07:30 PM||||Hey check this out, kids.  It turns out my sister's car just blew up.  The car is a 86 Lebarron turbo.  I guess something flammable (maybe the wiring harness) fell on to the hot turbo, and caught the engine on fire.  Fortunatly, my sister was parked in front of a construction site where men were quickly on the scene with fire extinguishers.  The car is totalled, and I have tools  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Now I know this has been discussed many times, but is that a Garrett T-03 under there?  I was set on nitrous, but the 'unfortunate' turn of events has got me thinking turbo again.  Even if I don't use it, I will give it to one of you guys.  What do you think? "TURBO 3.1" sorta has a nice ring to it. ||||reg||12
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||06-11-2001||08:14 PM||||Eric, I don't know for sure that what is under there is a T-03. But if it is and you don't want to use it, Let me have first dibs on it. I am installin a 3.4L and was thinking real hard about going Turbo. Let me know what you find. And to all you other VULTURES....BACK OFF!!!! IT"S MINE!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||06-11-2001||09:24 PM||||Was this Kari's car?? <P>Ha, and people think Fieros are flammable!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||06-11-2001||09:51 PM||||Yeah, that was Kari's car.  Our grandmother gave it to her a few years ago, and she just trashed it.  Maggie was the one who was driving though when it went poof.  I ended up standing out there on the road for better than an hour because I couldn't get my damn Sprint PCS phone to work so I could call a tow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>The highway trooper was pretty cool though.  He made a couple wisecracks about Maggie's driving then started asking questions about the Fiero.  I never thought the LAW would give me so much appreciation.  I even showed him the fire exinguisher I keep in front of the passenger's seat.  A Fiero coming to the rescue of a charred Lebarron, now that's irony.<P>I may end up using the spare peices of exhaust y-pipe I have laying around to try and fashion a turbo exhaust setup.  The biggest problem I see will be getting enough fuel to it.  I've got a set of 19lb mustang injectors, so I guess I just need a chip burned for my requirements.<P>Stay cool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||06-11-2001||10:08 PM||||watch the Sprint PCS remarks!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||onfire||06-12-2001||03:29 AM||||I hope you don't have the Samsung SCH-3500 that has to be the worst phone they have. That is the one I started out with, and I could get no kind of reception with it. Once I was even standing about 100 yards from a cel phone tower. So I took it back after only having it for about 2 weeks. Now I have Samsung SCH-8500 it cost a $50 more but its 10 times the phone. I have had no problems with it.<BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||06-12-2001||04:15 AM||||It's a T-29 I believe. To give you an idea , a 300ZX TT uses 2 of them , so it's not big enough for a 2.8+ engine.<P>No big deal really , go to a wrecker and find a merkur or T Bird turbo with a T3 turbo. As long as the housing is good , you can get a turbo rebuild kit from turbo city for under $100. With basic mechanical knowledge you can install it all. There good for 15+ psi of boost. They have a fixed wastegate , but that can be fixed. I had one running on my old merkur at 18psi boost with an intercooler. The inside of the turbo had been polished to spool up faster. Fun car.<P>The big thing with Fiero Turbo's isn't the turbo itself. T-3's are dime a dozen , it's the plumbing to put one on a Fiero that is a headache.<P>There are lots of posts about home grown turbo's , just do a search. The authority seems to be Dennis Lagrua, while he is not a forum member (I don't think) he is quite knowledgeable having built a turbo system for under a grand , and always willing to answer questions.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000007||85Josh||06-12-2001||03:33 PM||||I'll second Slammed's remarks. I can often find turbos for under $100 at a junkyard. I spoke to Dennis Lagrua at the Alabama swap meet, he spent about an hour answering questions, even though he knew I was asking about a four cylinder. Good luck, and have fun!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
